<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adam Opel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1837–1895</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adam Opel was a German industrialist who founded the company that bears his name. Trained as a locksmith, he began making sewing machines at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russelsheim">Rüsselsheim</a> in the Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> in 1862 and later added bicycles. After his death his sons began building motor cars in 1899, and Opel became one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s leading carmakers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adam-opel.jpg" alt="Adam Opel" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adam_Opel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
